1
00:00:00,520 --> 00:00:02,040
Did you want to kill Jarvis?

2
00:00:02,320 --> 00:00:05,320
I don't know what you mean.

3
00:00:05,600 --> 00:00:06,800
I'll post the video online.

4
00:00:06,880 --> 00:00:08,920
Let the Police find out what you
and your daughter did.

5
00:00:09,120 --> 00:00:12,720
I already told you, it's YIO, not IOY.

6
00:00:12,880 --> 00:00:14,000
Didn't you say Helen told you

7
00:00:14,120 --> 00:00:18,480
YIO stands for a high school group
called Youth Investment Organization?

8
00:00:18,640 --> 00:00:19,720
Why did it become IOY?

9
00:01:38,760 --> 00:01:40,360
Wendy, what is it?

10
00:01:40,640 --> 00:01:42,360
What are you doing here?

11
00:01:42,680 --> 00:01:43,600
See for yourself.

12
00:01:43,880 --> 00:01:46,960
I don't want anyone else to get hurt
from your pranks.

13
00:01:47,080 --> 00:01:49,560
If you feel a shred of guilt
for paralyzing me...

14
00:01:50,720 --> 00:01:52,280
I think you're quite mistaken.

15
00:01:52,600 --> 00:01:54,000
I don't feel guilty at all.

16
00:01:54,600 --> 00:01:56,600
Did you want to kill Jarvis?

17
00:01:56,880 --> 00:01:59,960
I don't know what you mean.

18
00:02:00,240 --> 00:02:01,920
Helen is your daughter.

19
00:02:02,040 --> 00:02:04,960
No wonder you quit right after Jarvis died.

20
00:02:05,160 --> 00:02:06,760
Even if he paralyzed your daughter,

21
00:02:06,840 --> 00:02:09,120
there's no need to kill him.

22
00:02:09,400 --> 00:02:11,920
Just because you found that video,

23
00:02:12,120 --> 00:02:13,760
you can't accuse me of murder.

24
00:02:13,840 --> 00:02:16,680
I really don't know what you mean.

25
00:02:16,920 --> 00:02:20,000
You won't admit it? I'll post it online.

26
00:02:20,120 --> 00:02:22,480
Let the Police find out what you
and your daughter did.

27
00:02:22,720 --> 00:02:23,520
No!

28
00:02:23,840 --> 00:02:25,560
(The truth about Ngai Ka-yan's death)

29
00:02:26,040 --> 00:02:28,120
Cheong, there's a new post on J Weekly.

30
00:02:28,320 --> 00:02:31,680
What? Ngai Ka-yan has just died.

31
00:02:32,360 --> 00:02:34,160
I attended most of the
Alumni Association functions...

32
00:02:34,240 --> 00:02:35,120
The truth about Ngai Ka-yan's death?

33
00:02:35,240 --> 00:02:36,520
Who's that girl?

34
00:02:38,600 --> 00:02:39,680
No!

35
00:02:40,000 --> 00:02:40,880
Let go!

36
00:02:41,200 --> 00:02:44,240
Give me the phone.

37
00:02:44,680 --> 00:02:46,240
This place hasn't changed much.

38
00:02:46,640 --> 00:02:49,360
The teachers who taught us are gone.

39
00:02:49,720 --> 00:02:50,600
Let go!

40
00:02:53,520 --> 00:02:56,080
I kicked a football tied to a fishing line.

41
00:02:56,400 --> 00:03:00,560
I landed on my back and became paralyzed.

42
00:03:01,200 --> 00:03:03,960
What happened? It stopped?

43
00:03:05,320 --> 00:03:06,680
It was deleted!

44
00:03:07,280 --> 00:03:08,280
Did you hear that?

45
00:03:08,640 --> 00:03:12,480
The girl mentioned a football and
she was paralyzed.

46
00:03:12,880 --> 00:03:14,280
That was obviously Lok Hiu-sin.

47
00:03:14,360 --> 00:03:16,720
This video was uploaded using
the J Weekly account.

48
00:03:16,880 --> 00:03:19,240
It's likely done by someone from
the online channel.

49
00:03:19,680 --> 00:03:23,080
They want us to know there's more
to the case.

50
00:03:23,520 --> 00:03:26,200
But why upload it and delete it right away?

51
00:03:27,920 --> 00:03:30,760
None of these can last too long.

52
00:03:31,080 --> 00:03:32,640
Luckily we ran into each other

53
00:03:32,760 --> 00:03:35,720
and you told me you're going abroad
with your Mom for your treatment.

54
00:03:35,880 --> 00:03:38,520
Or these would have gone to waste.

55
00:03:38,720 --> 00:03:40,080
Take them all if you can use them.

56
00:03:40,280 --> 00:03:41,400
Thank you.

57
00:03:42,040 --> 00:03:44,760
Don't worry, if I can't use them
or have leftovers,

58
00:03:44,840 --> 00:03:46,320
I'll take them to the food bank.

59
00:03:49,280 --> 00:03:52,000
What's this? It's rattling inside.

60
00:03:55,720 --> 00:03:58,400
That's Mom's stuff, not cup noodles.

61
00:03:58,480 --> 00:04:00,920
She wants it. Please put it back.

62
00:04:01,040 --> 00:04:03,160
Sorry, I'll put it back.

63
00:04:10,240 --> 00:04:11,360
Auntie Ching, I just came from your house...

64
00:04:11,480 --> 00:04:15,000
Hey...she blew me off!

65
00:04:23,440 --> 00:04:24,520
Get in!

66
00:04:26,240 --> 00:04:28,960
Yuen Kit-ching, you murderer! Open up!

67
00:04:29,280 --> 00:04:31,280
What are you doing? Open the door...

68
00:04:34,560 --> 00:04:38,080
Yuen Kit-ching, you murderer! Open the door!

69
00:04:40,000 --> 00:04:42,280
Oh dear! She said she kept a copy.

70
00:04:42,360 --> 00:04:45,760
That means she can show it again. I'm dead.

71
00:04:48,200 --> 00:04:49,640
Mom, Mrs. Chan was just here...

72
00:04:49,760 --> 00:04:52,120
Stop talking. Let's go to the airport now.

73
00:04:53,480 --> 00:04:54,800
But we're leaving tomorrow night.

74
00:04:55,040 --> 00:04:58,160
There's no time. We'll change our flight
at the airport.

75
00:04:58,280 --> 00:04:59,800
We must leave tonight.

76
00:05:00,080 --> 00:05:01,440
You haven't packed?

77
00:05:02,360 --> 00:05:03,360
I'll help you pack.

78
00:05:05,040 --> 00:05:08,000
Don't worry, everything uploaded
using our streaming platform

79
00:05:08,120 --> 00:05:09,760
will have a copy on the server.

80
00:05:09,960 --> 00:05:13,440
Only if I keep pulling pranks
on people without end,

81
00:05:15,200 --> 00:05:17,400
will I be able to live up to the past
eight years you have been paralyzed.

82
00:05:17,560 --> 00:05:20,360
Ngai Ka-yan is full of crap even after
he paralyzed someone.

83
00:05:20,520 --> 00:05:21,920
He's a genuine scumbag.

84
00:05:22,200 --> 00:05:24,200
Whoever uploaded this video
wants us to know

85
00:05:24,280 --> 00:05:26,440
Lok Hiu-sin has a motive to
kill Ngai Ka-yan.

86
00:05:27,520 --> 00:05:28,440
Let's bring her in.

87
00:05:29,240 --> 00:05:31,720
Police! We're looking for Miss Lok Hiu-sin.

88
00:05:31,960 --> 00:05:33,800
Helen? She's leaving soon.

89
00:05:34,040 --> 00:05:35,120
Leaving? Where to?

90
00:05:35,320 --> 00:05:37,760
Switzerland. Her flight was tomorrow.

91
00:05:37,960 --> 00:05:39,800
But she just changed it to tonight.

92
00:05:47,400 --> 00:05:48,040
Thanks.

93
00:05:48,440 --> 00:05:50,320
The university just came out with
their duty roster.

94
00:05:50,480 --> 00:05:51,920
Auntie Ching is on it.

95
00:05:52,120 --> 00:05:53,000
Let's head out to the airport.

96
00:06:03,280 --> 00:06:04,800
Thank you...

97
00:06:14,880 --> 00:06:17,000
Sin, no matter what happens,

98
00:06:17,120 --> 00:06:18,600
you must get on that plane.

99
00:06:18,760 --> 00:06:19,640
What about you?

100
00:06:19,840 --> 00:06:21,000
I'll join you later.

101
00:06:21,080 --> 00:06:21,960
No!

102
00:06:22,120 --> 00:06:24,720
Listen to me, you must leave.

103
00:06:25,040 --> 00:06:28,200
Yuen Kit-ching, stay where you are!

104
00:06:28,760 --> 00:06:29,600
Yuen Kit-ching, Lok Hiu-sin,

105
00:06:29,840 --> 00:06:31,480
we suspect you're involved in
Ngai Ka-yan's murder.

106
00:06:31,600 --> 00:06:33,360
We need you down at the station
to facilitate our investigation.

107
00:06:34,800 --> 00:06:39,280
Sir, my daughter must leave.

108
00:06:39,440 --> 00:06:41,840
I beg you to let us go.

109
00:06:41,920 --> 00:06:43,760
You won't get away. Stop this.

110
00:06:45,560 --> 00:06:49,120
Let me see her to the boarding gate.

111
00:06:55,680 --> 00:06:58,280
Auntie Ching, stop.

112
00:06:58,440 --> 00:06:59,600
Or you'll be resisting arrest.

113
00:07:05,400 --> 00:07:08,560
You did everything for your daughter.

114
00:07:09,920 --> 00:07:11,080
Don't make any more mistakes.

115
00:07:15,280 --> 00:07:16,280
Mom...

116
00:07:19,160 --> 00:07:20,960
Yuen Kit-ching, you're under arrest.

117
00:07:24,280 --> 00:07:26,400
You're anxious to leave town,

118
00:07:26,560 --> 00:07:27,920
is it because during the
Static Apnea Challenge,

119
00:07:28,120 --> 00:07:31,800
you swapped Ngai Ka-yan's oxygen
cylinder into H2S?

120
00:07:31,960 --> 00:07:34,720
You murdered him, that's why you
fled from justice?

121
00:07:35,160 --> 00:07:36,240
I didn't kill anyone.

122
00:07:37,600 --> 00:07:39,960
I'm not running away.

123
00:07:40,680 --> 00:07:45,280
I'm taking my daughter to Switzerland
for treatment.

124
00:07:45,840 --> 00:07:47,720
He paralyzed your daughter.

125
00:07:48,040 --> 00:07:49,680
Don't you want revenge?

126
00:07:50,320 --> 00:07:53,680
Whenever I think of my daughter's injury,

127
00:07:56,680 --> 00:07:59,080
it really breaks my heart.

128
00:08:00,280 --> 00:08:01,960
(Eight years ago)

129
00:08:02,440 --> 00:08:06,280
Doctor, I'm Lok Hiu-sin's mother.

130
00:08:06,440 --> 00:08:08,720
How is she?

131
00:08:09,000 --> 00:08:10,840
Your daughter had an accident
while playing football

132
00:08:11,120 --> 00:08:12,760
and injured her spinal nerves.

133
00:08:13,400 --> 00:08:14,560
The worst scenario is

134
00:08:14,720 --> 00:08:16,200
she may be paralyzed from the waist down.

135
00:08:16,640 --> 00:08:17,720
We'll do our best.

136
00:08:35,520 --> 00:08:36,240
Mom!

137
00:08:37,400 --> 00:08:40,480
I'm sorry, I slipped while playing football

138
00:08:40,640 --> 00:08:41,840
and ended up like this.

139
00:08:42,440 --> 00:08:45,960
Well? How do you feel?

140
00:08:46,240 --> 00:08:48,400
Does it hurt anywhere?

141
00:08:48,760 --> 00:08:54,960
Not really. My legs can't feel anything.

142
00:08:55,240 --> 00:08:57,040
Maybe the anesthetic hasn't worn off.

143
00:08:57,680 --> 00:09:01,880
Oh dear, the try out for the
Hong Kong team is next week.

144
00:09:02,000 --> 00:09:03,720
I wonder if I could get well in time.

145
00:09:07,520 --> 00:09:08,560
What's wrong, Mom?

146
00:09:09,400 --> 00:09:13,040
Nothing. I'm just worried.

147
00:09:14,600 --> 00:09:19,320
I promise I'll be there for you.

148
00:09:19,760 --> 00:09:25,400
You'll get well one day at a time.

149
00:09:27,360 --> 00:09:30,600
I only found out eight years later,

150
00:09:30,840 --> 00:09:32,800
it was Jarvis who paralyzed her.

151
00:09:33,200 --> 00:09:35,280
Exactly! After you found out,

152
00:09:35,400 --> 00:09:38,280
you were so angry you wanted to kill him.

153
00:09:38,560 --> 00:09:42,480
Yes, I was angry.

154
00:09:43,280 --> 00:09:46,200
But I would never kill him.

155
00:09:46,680 --> 00:09:49,000
We checked the serial number
of the cylinder,

156
00:09:49,200 --> 00:09:53,280
it matched the lot from the HKIU lab.

157
00:09:53,600 --> 00:09:57,400
You worked there part-time

158
00:09:57,640 --> 00:09:59,720
and quit right after the accident.

159
00:09:59,920 --> 00:10:01,400
How do you explain that?

160
00:10:04,760 --> 00:10:07,080
I have nothing to explain.

161
00:10:08,080 --> 00:10:10,400
I haven't finished grade school.

162
00:10:10,680 --> 00:10:13,840
I know nothing about chemistry.

163
00:10:14,640 --> 00:10:16,120
My daughter is paralyzed,

164
00:10:16,640 --> 00:10:18,840
and there's a new technology

165
00:10:19,000 --> 00:10:21,600
that may help her walk again.

166
00:10:21,960 --> 00:10:26,160
I quit my job so I can go with her
for the treatment.

167
00:10:26,240 --> 00:10:28,640
What's wrong with that?

168
00:10:29,600 --> 00:10:32,960
Lok Hiu-sin, we found out
Ngai Ka-yan paralyzed you.

169
00:10:33,160 --> 00:10:36,880
Is that why you colluded with your Mom
to kill him?

170
00:10:37,840 --> 00:10:39,920
It's true I have a beef with him.

171
00:10:40,120 --> 00:10:41,560
But that doesn't mean I'll kill him.

172
00:10:42,320 --> 00:10:45,880
I was injured the day of the livestreaming,

173
00:10:45,960 --> 00:10:47,360
I was resting at home.

174
00:10:47,960 --> 00:10:51,240
I found this pin in Ngai Ka-yan's office.

175
00:10:51,360 --> 00:10:55,200
It bears the same logo as the pendant
on the bracelet

176
00:10:55,280 --> 00:10:57,960
you wore when you recorded the TV show.

177
00:10:58,040 --> 00:11:01,720
Did you drop it when you swapped the
cylinders in Ngai Ka-yan's office?

178
00:11:02,040 --> 00:11:03,640
I was never at the channel office.

179
00:11:03,960 --> 00:11:08,120
This pin is from a high school club.

180
00:11:08,360 --> 00:11:09,280
What kind of club?

181
00:11:10,200 --> 00:11:14,080
Youth Investment Organization.

182
00:11:14,840 --> 00:11:18,840
The logo is the overlapping of Y, I and O.

183
00:11:19,240 --> 00:11:21,280
They made several souvenirs.

184
00:11:21,560 --> 00:11:23,560
Bracelets and pins.

185
00:11:24,000 --> 00:11:26,240
Ngai Ka-yan and I both joined this club.

186
00:11:26,440 --> 00:11:28,080
That's why we have souvenirs.

187
00:11:39,560 --> 00:11:40,560
Thank you.

188
00:11:41,880 --> 00:11:43,320
Lok Hiu-sin was right.

189
00:11:43,520 --> 00:11:46,880
Youth Investment Organization does exist.

190
00:11:47,040 --> 00:11:48,800
Lok Hiu-sin joined the sixth year,

191
00:11:48,960 --> 00:11:50,280
Ngai Ka-yan was the fourth.

192
00:11:50,560 --> 00:11:53,200
Maybe Ngai Ka-yan dropped the pin

193
00:11:53,280 --> 00:11:54,200
and not the killer?

194
00:11:54,400 --> 00:11:55,640
I went over all the statements.

195
00:11:55,760 --> 00:11:58,120
No one at the channel has seen
Ngai Ka-yan wearing this pin.

196
00:11:58,400 --> 00:12:01,200
It looked fairly new when I found it
in Ngai Ka-yan's office.

197
00:12:01,320 --> 00:12:02,560
Must have happened recently.

198
00:12:02,840 --> 00:12:06,440
Maybe someone picked up Ngai Ka-yan's pin

199
00:12:06,560 --> 00:12:08,280
and dropped it without knowing it.

200
00:12:08,480 --> 00:12:10,160
Most probably it's Auntie Ching.

201
00:12:10,280 --> 00:12:11,320
She took her daughter's pin

202
00:12:11,480 --> 00:12:13,280
and dropped it when she swapped
the cylinders.

203
00:12:13,480 --> 00:12:16,240
Let's not rule out Auntie Ching acted alone

204
00:12:16,360 --> 00:12:17,520
and Lok Hiu-sin knew nothing.

205
00:12:17,640 --> 00:12:20,400
No, the mother brought the daughter
to go on the run.

206
00:12:20,480 --> 00:12:21,800
The daughter is in the know.

207
00:12:22,040 --> 00:12:23,680
But they won't admit anything.

208
00:12:24,320 --> 00:12:25,240
Let them go.

209
00:12:25,600 --> 00:12:28,080
What? We still have plenty of time.

210
00:12:28,240 --> 00:12:30,160
We'll shake them up a bit longer.

211
00:12:30,240 --> 00:12:31,960
Maybe they'll spill the beans.

212
00:12:32,360 --> 00:12:35,520
We have no new evidence. Let her go.

213
00:12:37,920 --> 00:12:41,040
Miss Lok, there are seats on a flight
tonight to Switzerland via London.

214
00:12:41,160 --> 00:12:42,440
Will you consider it?

215
00:12:42,680 --> 00:12:45,400
Give me time to think.

216
00:12:45,680 --> 00:12:48,280
I see. Just a reminder,

217
00:12:48,440 --> 00:12:50,760
the plane takes off in four hours.

218
00:12:50,880 --> 00:12:52,120
If you decide to take it,

219
00:12:52,280 --> 00:12:54,240
you'll need to leave for the airport now
to check-in.

220
00:12:55,400 --> 00:12:57,440
Sin, no matter what happens,

221
00:12:57,600 --> 00:12:59,000
you must get on that plane.

222
00:12:59,240 --> 00:12:59,920
What about you?

223
00:13:00,040 --> 00:13:01,160
I'll join you later.

224
00:13:01,280 --> 00:13:02,360
No!

225
00:13:02,640 --> 00:13:04,680
Listen to me, you must leave.

226
00:13:18,920 --> 00:13:20,960
Brilliant, Gogo Sir!

227
00:13:21,240 --> 00:13:23,680
Lok Hiu-sin came back here.

228
00:13:24,280 --> 00:13:26,480
We have no new evidence. Let her go.

229
00:13:26,920 --> 00:13:29,760
Just like that? What if they run away again?

230
00:13:30,080 --> 00:13:32,280
Lok Hiu-sin is close to her mother.

231
00:13:32,400 --> 00:13:33,360
She would not leave her behind.

232
00:13:34,000 --> 00:13:35,520
If you were Lok Hiu-sin,

233
00:13:35,600 --> 00:13:37,360
what would you do when you got out?

234
00:13:37,520 --> 00:13:39,400
She'll do anything

235
00:13:39,520 --> 00:13:42,120
to destroy incriminating evidence
against her mother.

236
00:13:42,280 --> 00:13:44,960
Five cylinders were missing from
the university lab.

237
00:13:45,200 --> 00:13:47,000
If they had them,

238
00:13:47,160 --> 00:13:48,720
she'll find a way to dispose of them.

239
00:13:48,920 --> 00:13:51,080
When she comes downstairs with the evidence,

240
00:13:51,200 --> 00:13:53,480
we'll catch her red-handed.

241
00:13:56,320 --> 00:13:59,960
Ko Sir, that guy looks familiar.

242
00:14:02,960 --> 00:14:04,160
He's my ex-boyfriend.

243
00:14:04,640 --> 00:14:05,720
We used to live together.

244
00:14:06,000 --> 00:14:06,960
I was not well that day,

245
00:14:07,160 --> 00:14:08,480
he came by to keep me company.

246
00:14:08,920 --> 00:14:10,480
That's Lok Hiu-sin's boyfriend.

247
00:14:13,480 --> 00:14:15,040
What's so urgent that you needed
me here right away?

248
00:14:25,040 --> 00:14:26,000
What's wrong?

249
00:14:28,360 --> 00:14:30,720
I shouldn't have asked you to come up.

250
00:14:31,800 --> 00:14:33,800
But you're leaving next week.

251
00:14:34,160 --> 00:14:35,880
There's no telling when you'll be back.

252
00:14:36,520 --> 00:14:38,080
I want to see you one last time.

253
00:14:38,800 --> 00:14:41,240
Silly. Don't say these things.

254
00:14:43,400 --> 00:14:45,920
I'm not sure if I'll get another chance
to say this.

255
00:14:47,000 --> 00:14:48,680
I really want you to know

256
00:14:49,960 --> 00:14:52,400
I don't want to leave you.

257
00:14:53,960 --> 00:14:55,520
Did something happen?

258
00:14:57,640 --> 00:14:59,360
I prepared a present for you.

259
00:14:59,800 --> 00:15:01,200
It's on the shelf in the kitchen.

260
00:15:01,280 --> 00:15:02,720
Can you get it down?

261
00:15:11,480 --> 00:15:13,280
Lok Hiu-sin summoned the dude

262
00:15:13,600 --> 00:15:16,440
because she needs his help
to dispose of the cylinders.

263
00:15:21,720 --> 00:15:23,480
Bingo...

264
00:15:59,080 --> 00:16:00,640
You're giving me a case of cup noodles?

265
00:16:01,400 --> 00:16:04,440
No, I needed your help getting that down.

266
00:16:06,320 --> 00:16:07,360
Here's your present.

267
00:16:11,320 --> 00:16:14,400
Open it when you get home.

268
00:16:23,560 --> 00:16:24,440
Give it up.

269
00:16:28,480 --> 00:16:31,480
I thought Ching could help stall you.

270
00:16:31,920 --> 00:16:33,760
Your plan would have worked.

271
00:16:34,240 --> 00:16:37,040
But your boyfriend unwrapped the
present early.

272
00:16:38,960 --> 00:16:41,560
Cheong, stay on his tail.

273
00:17:02,960 --> 00:17:03,480
Hello?

274
00:17:03,800 --> 00:17:05,360
The bag only has a picture frame.

275
00:17:05,480 --> 00:17:06,560
There were no cylinders inside.

276
00:17:09,120 --> 00:17:11,120
You better tell us the whole story.

277
00:17:16,920 --> 00:17:20,240
Madam, you're too kind to walk me
to my cell.

278
00:17:20,400 --> 00:17:23,240
Shut up and get in.

279
00:17:23,560 --> 00:17:25,240
Aren't we crowded today?

280
00:17:25,320 --> 00:17:26,840
An auntie and a crippled girl.

281
00:17:29,200 --> 00:17:31,200
What does she look like?

282
00:17:31,280 --> 00:17:32,600
Is she in a wheelchair?

283
00:17:32,760 --> 00:17:36,400
Yes. She looks young. Why? You know her?

284
00:17:37,040 --> 00:17:39,480
We checked the serial number on the
cylinders you tried to toss.

285
00:17:39,680 --> 00:17:43,320
They were highly concentrated H2S stolen
from the HKIU lab.

286
00:17:43,680 --> 00:17:46,800
They were identical to the one Ngai Ka-yan
inhaled from.

287
00:17:47,040 --> 00:17:48,200
How do you explain that?

288
00:17:49,600 --> 00:17:51,440
The evidence we have indicates

289
00:17:51,600 --> 00:17:53,120
you and your Mom Yuen Kit-ching
conspired to commit murder.

290
00:17:53,400 --> 00:17:56,360
The act of disposing of the cylinders alone

291
00:17:56,480 --> 00:17:59,200
can nail you for conspiracy
to commit murder.

292
00:17:59,600 --> 00:18:00,840
It was entirely my own doing...

293
00:18:03,560 --> 00:18:05,040
Yuen Kit-ching is willing to testify.

294
00:18:11,640 --> 00:18:14,560
Sir, did you arrest my daughter?

295
00:18:14,640 --> 00:18:17,080
Where is she now? Can I see her?

296
00:18:17,400 --> 00:18:18,960
She's next door.

297
00:18:19,040 --> 00:18:19,960
My colleague is questioning her.

298
00:18:20,080 --> 00:18:23,840
I did it. She had nothing to do with this.

299
00:18:23,920 --> 00:18:25,480
Don't press charges against her.

300
00:18:25,720 --> 00:18:28,160
You daughter just admitted
everything was her doing.

301
00:18:28,320 --> 00:18:30,240
She helped you dispose of the
gas cylinders.

302
00:18:30,360 --> 00:18:31,680
Now you're taking the rap for everything.

303
00:18:32,080 --> 00:18:33,640
If you tell us the truth,

304
00:18:33,880 --> 00:18:35,200
maybe we can help you.

305
00:18:35,520 --> 00:18:37,600
She really has nothing to do with it.

306
00:18:37,680 --> 00:18:41,320
It was me. I planned the whole thing.

307
00:18:41,640 --> 00:18:46,520
My daughter would rather suffer
than be a burden to anyone.

308
00:18:46,560 --> 00:18:47,960
Why would she murder anyone?

309
00:18:48,640 --> 00:18:49,560
She may be paralyzed,

310
00:18:49,720 --> 00:18:51,880
but she has overcome so much.

311
00:18:51,960 --> 00:18:53,200
She finished college

312
00:18:53,520 --> 00:18:57,360
and has a boyfriend who sticks with her.

313
00:18:57,440 --> 00:18:58,600
(A week before the incident)

314
00:18:58,680 --> 00:19:00,960
I thought the worst was over.

315
00:19:01,680 --> 00:19:03,240
Then Ngai Ka-yan showed up

316
00:19:03,400 --> 00:19:05,400
and pushed her further down the abyss.

317
00:19:05,640 --> 00:19:09,560
Sin, what's wrong? Are you hurt?

318
00:19:09,800 --> 00:19:12,640
Don't help me. I can get up.

319
00:19:12,720 --> 00:19:16,760
Come on, let me help you, OK?

320
00:19:17,080 --> 00:19:19,480
I don't need any help.

321
00:19:19,960 --> 00:19:22,360
I don't want to be anyone's burden.

322
00:19:23,120 --> 00:19:25,520
I have been a drag to you and Ching
for too long.

323
00:19:26,080 --> 00:19:29,280
Dad left because I was a burden.

324
00:19:29,440 --> 00:19:34,840
No. I never considered you a burden.

325
00:19:35,080 --> 00:19:37,120
You have a steady job.

326
00:19:37,240 --> 00:19:39,280
You can support yourself and help others.

327
00:19:39,360 --> 00:19:41,000
You're quite brilliant.

328
00:19:41,200 --> 00:19:42,520
But what's the use?

329
00:19:42,680 --> 00:19:46,600
See? I need this wheelchair to get around.

330
00:19:46,800 --> 00:19:48,440
I had to haul the dialysis machine
everywhere I go.

331
00:19:48,520 --> 00:19:50,760
Tell me, what's the point?

332
00:19:51,240 --> 00:19:55,880
Sin, why are you so upset?

333
00:19:56,080 --> 00:19:57,720
Did something happen?

334
00:19:58,760 --> 00:19:59,840
If you're not feeling well,

335
00:19:59,960 --> 00:20:01,240
shall I take you to the doctor?

336
00:20:01,360 --> 00:20:04,960
Why bother? No more doctors.

337
00:20:05,040 --> 00:20:06,720
The world is so unfair.

338
00:20:07,000 --> 00:20:08,920
You and I work so hard,

339
00:20:09,240 --> 00:20:12,640
while Ngai Ka-yan hurt so many people
but he's doing better and better.

340
00:20:13,320 --> 00:20:16,920
Ngai Ka-yan? Jarvis, my Boss?

341
00:20:17,200 --> 00:20:19,040
I didn't paralyze myself in an accident.

342
00:20:19,160 --> 00:20:20,800
Ngai Ka-yan pulled a prank on me.

343
00:20:20,840 --> 00:20:22,160
He paralyzed me.

344
00:20:24,840 --> 00:20:26,040
How did that happen?

345
00:20:27,760 --> 00:20:29,120
How come?

346
00:20:31,040 --> 00:20:32,320
What did he do?

347
00:20:32,560 --> 00:20:35,520
I missed kicking the football and
landed on my back.

348
00:20:35,680 --> 00:20:39,080
Ngai Ka-yan pulled it away
with a fishing line.

349
00:20:39,120 --> 00:20:41,080
He paralyzed me.

350
00:20:41,440 --> 00:20:43,920
I can't believe I worked for him
for a few years,

351
00:20:44,080 --> 00:20:46,000
and he was the one who paralyzed
my daughter.

352
00:20:46,160 --> 00:20:49,600
Ngai Ka-yan, you scumbag!

353
00:20:50,200 --> 00:20:51,720
Auntie Ching, just put them down.

354
00:20:52,040 --> 00:20:53,800
I want to tell you the answer is no.

355
00:20:54,360 --> 00:20:57,600
I simply enjoy the pleasure of
pulling a prank on someone.

356
00:20:58,480 --> 00:21:01,040
I wanted to slap him so bad.

357
00:21:01,400 --> 00:21:03,440
But I know it won't do any good.

358
00:21:04,080 --> 00:21:06,080
He enjoys pulling pranks on others,

359
00:21:06,840 --> 00:21:10,400
he's bound to hurt Tom or someone else
during the livestreaming.

360
00:21:10,520 --> 00:21:13,280
I didn't know what to do.
What's this? It stinks!

361
00:21:13,560 --> 00:21:16,880
Then I stumbled upon something...

362
00:21:20,960 --> 00:21:23,280
Those two clowns were up to no good!

363
00:21:23,720 --> 00:21:27,000
No wonder when Wendy picked up
the cylinder, they overreacted.

364
00:21:30,320 --> 00:21:32,360
What are you doing? Don't touch it.

365
00:21:32,480 --> 00:21:34,720
I'm trying to see if it works.

366
00:21:34,920 --> 00:21:36,840
That's the oxygen for the
Static Apnea Challenge.

367
00:21:36,920 --> 00:21:38,880
Can you keep things tidy?

368
00:21:39,200 --> 00:21:41,480
It's a whole box of stink bombs.

369
00:21:42,120 --> 00:21:43,840
You want to embarrass me
in front of the camera?

370
00:21:44,920 --> 00:21:46,760
Where are those two losers?

371
00:21:50,480 --> 00:21:54,200
Wait...if I expose them now,
I'd be letting them off the hook.

372
00:21:55,920 --> 00:21:58,920
If they want to play games, I'm in.

373
00:21:59,240 --> 00:22:03,840
He never questioned why Tom and Paul
wanted to teach him a lesson.

374
00:22:04,040 --> 00:22:06,120
All he cared about was tricking others.

375
00:22:06,680 --> 00:22:09,720
People like him won't cry until
he sees his own coffin.

376
00:22:10,040 --> 00:22:12,880
But I couldn't think of a solution.

377
00:22:13,440 --> 00:22:15,680
Then I found something at the university...

378
00:22:15,960 --> 00:22:18,680
Is it OK to leave this lying around?

379
00:22:18,920 --> 00:22:20,640
Then we'll take it with us for our smoke.

380
00:22:20,720 --> 00:22:22,800
Are you crazy?

381
00:22:22,960 --> 00:22:24,920
This is highly concentrated H2S,

382
00:22:25,080 --> 00:22:27,120
a spark of fire will cause an explosion.

383
00:22:27,360 --> 00:22:28,560
Don't exaggerate.

384
00:22:28,680 --> 00:22:30,640
Have you heard of swamp gas?

385
00:22:30,720 --> 00:22:32,440
It's about the same.

386
00:22:32,600 --> 00:22:34,200
A whiff can kill you...

387
00:22:34,280 --> 00:22:35,680
When I overheard their conversation,

388
00:22:35,880 --> 00:22:37,760
the first thing that came to mind

389
00:22:37,960 --> 00:22:42,480
I was working part-time, filling in
for someone else.

390
00:22:42,560 --> 00:22:45,360
No one would know I stole the cylinder.

391
00:22:55,600 --> 00:22:57,080
(Biohazard)

392
00:22:59,680 --> 00:23:04,400
Oh dear, I forgot to clean Tim's office.

393
00:23:04,520 --> 00:23:05,360
How forgetful of me!

394
00:23:05,520 --> 00:23:06,960
Don't wait for me. You go ahead.

395
00:23:07,000 --> 00:23:08,440
I'll go back and clean up.

396
00:23:14,640 --> 00:23:16,040
I had a false sense of security,

397
00:23:16,280 --> 00:23:20,800
thinking it was Heaven's will
to help me avenge Sin.

398
00:23:22,240 --> 00:23:23,800
When I was stealing the cylinders,

399
00:23:24,120 --> 00:23:27,480
I noticed they have different
colors and labels.

400
00:23:28,240 --> 00:23:30,320
I didn't know which was which,

401
00:23:30,600 --> 00:23:32,840
so I took one from each box

402
00:23:33,000 --> 00:23:35,400
and will look them up later at home.

403
00:23:40,760 --> 00:23:42,200
Hydrogen sulfide.

404
00:23:44,720 --> 00:23:46,880
So these are not what I want.

405
00:24:05,920 --> 00:24:06,960
Come in!

406
00:24:08,680 --> 00:24:11,320
Mom, why did you hide in your room
right after dinner?

407
00:24:11,440 --> 00:24:12,120
You're not feeling well?

408
00:24:12,400 --> 00:24:16,440
No, I'm counting my money.

409
00:24:17,640 --> 00:24:20,400
What's up? You want to share
your secret with me?

410
00:24:21,120 --> 00:24:22,440
I've been thinking...

411
00:24:23,200 --> 00:24:25,360
I have decided to declare war
on Ngai Ka-yan.

412
00:24:26,080 --> 00:24:26,600
Good!

413
00:24:28,160 --> 00:24:29,920
After what the scumbag did to you,

414
00:24:30,640 --> 00:24:32,280
I won't let him off easy.

415
00:24:33,080 --> 00:24:36,000
Tell me, how do you want your revenge?

416
00:24:36,400 --> 00:24:38,920
I don't want revenge.

417
00:24:39,240 --> 00:24:40,680
But you said you want to declare war.

418
00:24:41,120 --> 00:24:44,480
I think...if he knew something
he did for fun,

419
00:24:44,840 --> 00:24:46,680
put me in a wheelchair,

420
00:24:47,480 --> 00:24:49,560
he might feel guilty and regret it.

421
00:24:49,840 --> 00:24:51,320
I intend to meet with him,

422
00:24:51,400 --> 00:24:54,200
stop him from hurting people again

423
00:24:54,360 --> 00:24:55,560
by stopping his pranks.

424
00:24:56,880 --> 00:24:58,280
Good!

425
00:24:59,640 --> 00:25:03,240
You should give him a chance.

426
00:25:03,800 --> 00:25:06,120
Right there, I dropped the idea
of killing him.

427
00:25:06,400 --> 00:25:08,840
I don't know if that scumbag would
listen to Hiu-sin,

428
00:25:08,960 --> 00:25:10,800
so I followed her to the school.

429
00:25:11,480 --> 00:25:13,600
Sure enough, he was a genuine scumbag.

430
00:25:14,000 --> 00:25:17,680
If you were destined to be paralyzed,
you still couldn't have dodged it.

431
00:25:18,080 --> 00:25:19,360
I'm not talking to a lunatic

432
00:25:23,160 --> 00:25:24,160
Yes!

433
00:25:25,800 --> 00:25:27,120
You're crazy!

434
00:25:27,440 --> 00:25:29,440
People get hurt in accidents every day.

435
00:25:29,840 --> 00:25:32,800
Should we just stay home and do nothing?

436
00:25:33,040 --> 00:25:35,720
How I wanted to stab and kill him
right then and there.

437
00:25:36,120 --> 00:25:40,040
But I told myself I must be patient.

438
00:25:40,200 --> 00:25:41,080
Morning, Auntie Ching...

439
00:25:41,160 --> 00:25:45,440
Because I can kill the scumbag without
anyone knowing about it.

440
00:25:46,280 --> 00:25:48,440
That day, I arrived at the channel
at 12 o'clock.

441
00:25:49,000 --> 00:25:51,200
Though I prepared the poison gas,

442
00:25:51,360 --> 00:25:54,080
I didn't know if Jarvis has swapped
the cylinder.

443
00:25:54,160 --> 00:25:55,400
So I couldn't do anything.

444
00:25:55,480 --> 00:25:56,280
Morning, everyone!

445
00:25:56,480 --> 00:25:57,160
Morning!

446
00:25:58,120 --> 00:25:59,920
That scumbag came in soon afterwards

447
00:26:00,160 --> 00:26:02,560
and greeted me in a happy mood.

448
00:26:03,120 --> 00:26:04,800
After he went inside his office,

449
00:26:04,960 --> 00:26:07,800
I saw him take out a gas cylinder
from his backpack.

450
00:26:08,480 --> 00:26:14,160
That must be the oxygen he planned to
use on Tom and Paul.

451
00:26:17,360 --> 00:26:19,320
He left soon afterwards.

452
00:26:19,760 --> 00:26:21,560
I heard he was meeting Daisy for lunch.

453
00:26:22,000 --> 00:26:25,360
He didn't take his backpack or
lock his office.

454
00:26:25,600 --> 00:26:28,720
I knew they were livestreaming
the Challenge after lunch.

455
00:26:29,000 --> 00:26:31,920
That was my only chance.

456
00:26:32,160 --> 00:26:36,960
But Paul and Wendy started their livecast
then and there.

457
00:26:37,400 --> 00:26:38,960
I went back to the pantry

458
00:26:39,160 --> 00:26:42,040
and waited for them to finish so I could
get into the office.

459
00:26:42,320 --> 00:26:45,400
As you can see...we have shredded paper.

460
00:26:45,560 --> 00:26:46,640
I'm not lying.

461
00:26:46,760 --> 00:26:48,920
But their show went on and on...

462
00:26:49,320 --> 00:26:51,360
I hope you'll like today's magic.

463
00:26:51,480 --> 00:26:53,320
Remember to CLS. See you next time...

464
00:26:55,160 --> 00:26:57,040
When they finally finished,

465
00:26:57,160 --> 00:26:59,720
I knew that was the best chance.

466
00:27:00,560 --> 00:27:03,720
I saw Wendy take out the garbage.

467
00:27:04,040 --> 00:27:05,720
Tom went into the conference room.

468
00:27:06,040 --> 00:27:08,200
I went in to swap the cylinders.

469
00:27:37,000 --> 00:27:39,600
At that moment, it dawned on me,

470
00:27:39,760 --> 00:27:43,160
after I left, this door will be
Jarvis' gate of Hell

471
00:27:43,640 --> 00:27:46,680
and I'll become a murderer.

472
00:27:47,240 --> 00:27:51,280
I hesitated. Do I really want to do this?

473
00:27:51,680 --> 00:27:54,040
Even if you can't catch me,

474
00:27:54,320 --> 00:27:56,720
I won't have peace of mind
for the rest of my life,

475
00:27:56,800 --> 00:28:00,120
or keep my head up in front of my daughter.

476
00:28:07,880 --> 00:28:09,160
Auntie Ching, something is broken.

477
00:28:09,240 --> 00:28:10,280
Can you clean that up?

478
00:28:10,720 --> 00:28:12,600
I was so scared.

479
00:28:12,840 --> 00:28:14,200
I was holding onto the cylinder,

480
00:28:14,360 --> 00:28:16,240
Paul wanted me to clean up something.

481
00:28:16,400 --> 00:28:19,280
I didn't want him to see me
holding the cylinder.

482
00:28:19,680 --> 00:28:22,440
So I stuck it behind the model

483
00:28:22,640 --> 00:28:24,160
and will try to get it back later.

484
00:28:34,640 --> 00:28:37,960
But the paint I got on my hand
can prove I was in the room,

485
00:28:38,120 --> 00:28:41,080
so I washed it off right away
in the toilet.

486
00:28:51,720 --> 00:28:53,360
I didn't see anyone when I came out.

487
00:28:53,800 --> 00:28:57,480
I wanted to get back into Jarvis' office
right away to get the cylinder.

488
00:28:57,720 --> 00:29:00,240
But Tom suddenly came out
from the men's room.

489
00:29:04,280 --> 00:29:06,640
Auntie Ching, I'll help you dump
this in the back stairs.

490
00:29:07,280 --> 00:29:08,400
Don't cut yourself.

491
00:29:17,600 --> 00:29:19,240
Tom, what are you doing here?

492
00:29:19,800 --> 00:29:20,560
You have nothing better to do?

493
00:29:21,000 --> 00:29:22,120
Get back in...

494
00:29:22,360 --> 00:29:25,200
Jarvis came back at that time.

495
00:29:25,400 --> 00:29:27,480
Paul, have you packed up everything?
It's almost 2 o'clock.

496
00:29:27,560 --> 00:29:28,960
Then he went back to his office.

497
00:29:29,040 --> 00:29:30,160
All set and ready to go.

498
00:29:30,560 --> 00:29:32,320
Go down for the set up. I'll be down later.

499
00:29:33,960 --> 00:29:36,800
Then I saw Daisy go into Jarvis' office.

500
00:29:37,000 --> 00:29:40,680
Soon afterwards, they left
with the backpack.

501
00:29:45,000 --> 00:29:47,600
Right then, I knew I'm in trouble.

502
00:29:47,960 --> 00:29:50,720
Only he has the key to the room.

503
00:29:51,000 --> 00:29:53,440
I couldn't go in to get the poison gas.

504
00:29:54,040 --> 00:29:56,640
After the accident, we went to the channel
to look for evidence.

505
00:29:56,800 --> 00:29:59,080
You were the only one there.

506
00:29:59,360 --> 00:30:01,160
Were you trying to retrieve the cylinder?

507
00:30:01,440 --> 00:30:07,160
Yes. I tried looking for the spare key.

508
00:30:07,360 --> 00:30:11,560
I couldn't get in and get the cylinder.

509
00:30:12,120 --> 00:30:16,440
When I heard Jarvis died from
inhaling poison gas,

510
00:30:16,880 --> 00:30:19,600
my heart almost skipped a beat.

511
00:30:19,680 --> 00:30:23,720
I kept wondering if I was involved.

512
00:30:23,920 --> 00:30:27,200
I swapped the cylinders back.

513
00:30:27,320 --> 00:30:30,880
Did Jarvis pick up the wrong one?

514
00:30:31,480 --> 00:30:35,880
Or did I mix them up?

515
00:30:37,160 --> 00:30:40,840
I wanted to know whether the one
behind the model was still there.

516
00:30:41,280 --> 00:30:43,800
I wasn't sure if you would find it.

517
00:30:44,360 --> 00:30:46,280
In the end, I didn't see it

518
00:30:46,720 --> 00:30:48,920
and you locked the door after you.

519
00:30:49,320 --> 00:30:51,680
When you started to suspect Tom and Paul,

520
00:30:52,320 --> 00:30:54,960
I consoled myself

521
00:30:57,080 --> 00:31:01,000
maybe Tom screwed up
when he prepared the cylinders.

522
00:31:01,640 --> 00:31:05,160
But I still felt uneasy.

523
00:31:05,440 --> 00:31:07,280
That's why you quit?

524
00:31:09,040 --> 00:31:11,120
Daisy later told me,

525
00:31:12,000 --> 00:31:17,480
she got the cylinder from Jarvis' backpack.

526
00:31:17,920 --> 00:31:21,800
I lost the last excuse I gave myself.

527
00:31:22,400 --> 00:31:25,360
I must have gotten them mixed up

528
00:31:25,800 --> 00:31:29,320
and Jarvis died from inhaling my cylinder.

529
00:31:29,880 --> 00:31:32,240
Why did you quit your university job?

530
00:31:34,720 --> 00:31:38,440
I know you'll find the source of
the poison gas sooner or later.

531
00:31:38,800 --> 00:31:42,000
I was just trying to buy time.

532
00:31:42,720 --> 00:31:46,840
I was hoping to go away with Sin.

533
00:31:47,400 --> 00:31:52,200
I just didn't expect Wendy to suspect me.

534
00:31:52,720 --> 00:31:53,840
Wendy?

535
00:31:54,240 --> 00:31:58,400
She got ahold of the video of
Sin and Jarvis at the playground.

536
00:31:58,600 --> 00:32:02,160
She figured out I wanted to kill Jarvis.

537
00:32:02,880 --> 00:32:06,080
I deleted the video
and headed out to the airport.

538
00:32:06,680 --> 00:32:08,840
I really thought I could get away.

539
00:32:09,280 --> 00:32:12,440
Were you wearing this pin on the
day in question?

540
00:32:15,520 --> 00:32:18,760
I don't like accessories.

541
00:32:19,360 --> 00:32:20,840
I have never seen it.

542
00:32:23,280 --> 00:32:26,520
I told you everything.

543
00:32:27,120 --> 00:32:30,360
Will my daughter be OK?

544
00:32:30,800 --> 00:32:32,920
We'll check out your story

545
00:32:33,080 --> 00:32:34,880
before we know if your daughter is involved.

546
00:32:37,680 --> 00:32:38,960
Get in!

547
00:32:41,720 --> 00:32:44,240
Mom!
Sin...

548
00:32:44,600 --> 00:32:46,480
Let go...

549
00:32:46,960 --> 00:32:53,400
Madam, please put me in this cell.

550
00:32:53,600 --> 00:32:56,280
She's my daughter. She has kidney problems.

551
00:32:56,400 --> 00:32:58,600
Let me watch over her.

552
00:32:58,680 --> 00:33:01,400
If anything should happen,
I can get help right away.

553
00:33:01,600 --> 00:33:03,720
Please, Madam?

554
00:33:04,280 --> 00:33:05,520
Over there! Come with me.

555
00:33:06,440 --> 00:33:07,160
Sin!

556
00:33:09,200 --> 00:33:11,760
Thank you, Madam! Thanks...

557
00:33:11,800 --> 00:33:13,280
Sin!
Mom!

558
00:33:14,360 --> 00:33:16,120
Why didn't you listen to me?

559
00:33:16,680 --> 00:33:19,240
Why didn't you get on the plane?

560
00:33:19,400 --> 00:33:22,120
I can't bear to see you spend
the rest of your life in here.

561
00:33:32,760 --> 00:33:35,560
Why didn't you get on the plane?

562
00:33:35,840 --> 00:33:38,760
I can't bear to see you spend
the rest of your life in here.

563
00:33:39,560 --> 00:33:43,280
The officer said even if you
didn't kill anyone,

564
00:33:43,880 --> 00:33:46,120
you tried to dispose of the cylinders.

565
00:33:46,440 --> 00:33:51,000
They're likely to charge you with
obstruction of justice.

566
00:33:51,440 --> 00:33:53,200
How could I be so careless

567
00:33:53,720 --> 00:33:56,040
and let you find those cylinders?

568
00:33:56,280 --> 00:33:59,640
Because you made me move back home.

569
00:34:02,920 --> 00:34:06,440
When I saw the box full of hydrogen sulfide,

570
00:34:06,840 --> 00:34:10,720
I knew you were connected to Jarvis' death.

571
00:34:11,280 --> 00:34:13,160
The whole box?

572
00:34:14,520 --> 00:34:17,720
I checked the words online.

573
00:34:18,000 --> 00:34:22,120
Only the cylinder I took was
hydrogen sulfide.

574
00:34:22,680 --> 00:34:26,080
Hydrogen sulfide is the name in English.

575
00:34:26,480 --> 00:34:29,600
Its molecular formula is H2S.

576
00:34:29,920 --> 00:34:32,800
It's highly concentrated.

577
00:34:33,520 --> 00:34:38,320
I was planning to return them
to the university.

578
00:34:38,440 --> 00:34:43,040
I thought they won't notice
one were missing.

579
00:34:44,160 --> 00:34:46,360
I meant to dispose of them for you.

580
00:34:47,080 --> 00:34:48,520
When I found them missing,

581
00:34:48,960 --> 00:34:50,320
I thought you got rid of them already.

582
00:34:50,600 --> 00:34:52,600
But you just put it on the shelf

583
00:34:52,880 --> 00:34:54,520
and Mrs. Chan almost found them.

584
00:34:55,960 --> 00:34:58,040
Since I found out your secret,

585
00:34:58,560 --> 00:35:01,000
I haven't been able to sleep.

586
00:35:01,720 --> 00:35:04,280
I was worried when I open my eyes
the next day,

587
00:35:04,560 --> 00:35:06,520
you would have been arrested by the Police.

588
00:35:07,200 --> 00:35:11,040
This is why you didn't tell me
your kidney deteriorated

589
00:35:11,360 --> 00:35:15,760
and tried to go places with me.

590
00:35:16,440 --> 00:35:20,880
You told me there's a new treatment
and it's free.

591
00:35:21,800 --> 00:35:25,480
You only wanted me to leave town.

592
00:35:26,680 --> 00:35:28,240
I should have planned it better.

593
00:35:29,080 --> 00:35:31,600
If I chased Switzerland harder,

594
00:35:31,720 --> 00:35:34,120
I really could have taken you away.

595
00:35:36,160 --> 00:35:40,280
Let it be. Even if we got away,

596
00:35:41,080 --> 00:35:43,320
I must still live with a guilty conscience.

597
00:35:44,960 --> 00:35:51,080
Mom, that scumbag is not worth it.

598
00:35:51,720 --> 00:35:53,880
You can't bear to see me suffer.

599
00:35:54,440 --> 00:35:57,720
How can I bear to see that scumbag
bully you?

600
00:35:58,560 --> 00:36:03,440
Actually...I wasn't thinking straight.

601
00:36:03,840 --> 00:36:06,120
I never intended to give up.

602
00:36:06,720 --> 00:36:08,560
Whatever that scumbag did to me,

603
00:36:08,720 --> 00:36:10,320
I will persist.

604
00:36:10,760 --> 00:36:16,400
We still have so much to do together.

605
00:36:17,320 --> 00:36:19,840
That's part of my experience in life.

606
00:36:25,480 --> 00:36:29,120
I will bear the consequences of my action.

607
00:36:32,400 --> 00:36:33,080
(Three months after the incident)

608
00:36:33,240 --> 00:36:35,840
The defendant of livestreaming murder
will be arraigned tomorrow.

609
00:36:36,240 --> 00:36:39,720
We didn't have enough to nail her.

610
00:36:40,040 --> 00:36:43,880
Luckily Gogo Sir had the nerve
to set a bait.

611
00:36:45,480 --> 00:36:48,320
What's on your mind? Auntie Ching
goes to court tomorrow.

612
00:36:49,200 --> 00:36:51,880
She admitted to everything,

613
00:36:52,000 --> 00:36:54,440
except dropping the pin.

614
00:36:54,880 --> 00:36:57,440
Gogo Sir, are you kidding me?

615
00:36:57,520 --> 00:36:59,400
You're still thinking about that
after three months?

616
00:36:59,560 --> 00:37:02,360
No wonder you seldom have tea
with us lately.

617
00:37:02,560 --> 00:37:05,280
Over-exertion won't help you think.

618
00:37:05,480 --> 00:37:07,720
Hurry up and finish your sandwich.

619
00:37:08,080 --> 00:37:10,400
Wait...shouldn't there be two pieces?

620
00:37:10,560 --> 00:37:11,680
How come there's only one left?

621
00:37:11,840 --> 00:37:13,000
You're not concentrating,

622
00:37:13,160 --> 00:37:15,040
you had no idea what you ate.

623
00:37:15,400 --> 00:37:17,960
I only heard you talk about

624
00:37:18,160 --> 00:37:19,960
who swapped the cylinders.

625
00:37:20,080 --> 00:37:21,360
I got so bored listening to that.

626
00:37:21,640 --> 00:37:22,640
Can't you talk about something else?

627
00:37:23,000 --> 00:37:25,960
There's something I want to ask you.

628
00:37:26,520 --> 00:37:29,040
Did you think of something?

629
00:37:29,360 --> 00:37:31,720
Didn't you say someone broke a vase?

630
00:37:31,880 --> 00:37:32,440
Yes!

631
00:37:33,760 --> 00:37:36,560
Was it expensive?

632
00:37:38,440 --> 00:37:40,560
And I thought you had a new angle.

633
00:37:41,320 --> 00:37:44,040
What a shame if someone broke
an antique vase.

634
00:37:44,160 --> 00:37:45,080
It must be expensive.

635
00:37:45,480 --> 00:37:48,120
How come whoever broke it
didn't have to pay for it?

636
00:37:48,200 --> 00:37:48,960
That's odd.

637
00:37:49,400 --> 00:37:51,960
Besides, breaking a vase was so loud,

638
00:37:52,080 --> 00:37:53,120
how come nobody heard the bang?

639
00:37:53,600 --> 00:37:57,480
You're right! How come nobody
heard the noise?

640
00:37:58,080 --> 00:38:00,840
I heard the door open and close.

641
00:38:01,160 --> 00:38:02,840
Someone must have come in and went out.

642
00:38:03,920 --> 00:38:05,640
When the vase was broken,

643
00:38:05,840 --> 00:38:07,920
Auntie Ching should be inside
Ngai Ka-yan's office.

644
00:38:09,480 --> 00:38:12,240
Auntie Ching was worried the paint
could prove she was in the room,

645
00:38:12,400 --> 00:38:14,880
so she went to the toilet to wash her hands.

646
00:38:17,680 --> 00:38:19,480
After you threw out the garbage,

647
00:38:19,600 --> 00:38:20,680
did you go straight to the toilet?

648
00:38:20,840 --> 00:38:21,840
Or did you go somewhere else?

649
00:38:22,040 --> 00:38:23,800
Because I had makeup in my bag,

650
00:38:24,000 --> 00:38:25,840
I went straight to the toilet.

651
00:38:26,280 --> 00:38:28,120
Did you hear any weird noises outside?

652
00:38:28,400 --> 00:38:29,360
No.

653
00:38:30,440 --> 00:38:33,440
Daisy said one person went into the toilet,

654
00:38:33,840 --> 00:38:36,920
but both Auntie Ching and Wendy
claimed they were in there.

655
00:38:45,560 --> 00:38:48,880
Wendy, you're lying.

656
00:38:49,520 --> 00:38:51,120
You couldn't have been to the toilet.

657
00:38:51,400 --> 00:38:53,480
Where were you at the time?

658
00:38:54,680 --> 00:38:59,760
Did you break the vase and kill Ngai Ka-yan?

659
00:39:01,920 --> 00:39:04,440
Based on your analysis,
Wendy is the real killer?

660
00:39:04,720 --> 00:39:05,920
I can't be sure.

661
00:39:06,120 --> 00:39:09,560
We can't rule out the possibility of
her lying for other reasons.

662
00:39:10,160 --> 00:39:12,360
Before we find other leads,

663
00:39:12,920 --> 00:39:14,160
everything is just talk.

664
00:39:14,560 --> 00:39:17,120
If we still have doubts,
why are we still charging Auntie Ching?

665
00:39:17,320 --> 00:39:19,680
Because she admitted everything.

666
00:39:19,800 --> 00:39:21,520
Circumstantial evidence is against her.

667
00:39:21,720 --> 00:39:25,720
I still think the case has too many
questionable points.

668
00:39:25,840 --> 00:39:26,880
(Brand new prankster channel)

669
00:39:31,120 --> 00:39:32,760
(A channel tailor made for Hong Kongers)

670
00:39:33,280 --> 00:39:35,040
What's this? It stinks.

671
00:39:35,480 --> 00:39:36,720
(Brand new program)

672
00:39:37,200 --> 00:39:39,880
Arrest me...
Bust me, officer...

673
00:39:39,960 --> 00:39:41,120
(Brand new cast)

674
00:39:45,560 --> 00:39:46,840
(Brand new name)

675
00:39:47,320 --> 00:39:48,880
(Stay tuned for IOY Channel)

676
00:39:48,920 --> 00:39:51,240
These three videos were shot by Agent J.

677
00:39:51,360 --> 00:39:52,800
Is this a new logo?

678
00:39:53,200 --> 00:39:56,000
You said Lok Hiu-sin told you
these alphabets stand for

679
00:39:56,120 --> 00:39:59,280
a high school group called
Youth Investment Organization.

680
00:39:59,440 --> 00:40:01,080
Why did it become IOY?

681
00:40:02,680 --> 00:40:05,960
IOY Channel will livestream in ten minutes.

682
00:40:06,200 --> 00:40:07,840
Those who want to watch,

683
00:40:08,040 --> 00:40:09,400
use the toilet now and grab your popcorn.

684
00:40:09,760 --> 00:40:11,520
See you later.

685
00:40:12,080 --> 00:40:12,920
Let's go check it out.

686
00:40:13,040 --> 00:40:13,680
Right!

687
00:40:15,200 --> 00:40:16,720
By following their livestreaming,

688
00:40:16,880 --> 00:40:18,520
they should be somewhere around here.

689
00:40:25,440 --> 00:40:27,800
Wake up...

690
00:40:31,520 --> 00:40:36,760
Get him...
He can't get up...

691
00:40:37,000 --> 00:40:39,280
Stop it! You think this is fun?

692
00:40:40,320 --> 00:40:42,160
That's what we like, butt out!

693
00:40:42,360 --> 00:40:44,600
You swallowed dynamite
or having your period?

694
00:40:44,840 --> 00:40:46,600
Maybe it stopped...

695
00:40:46,920 --> 00:40:49,400
Looks like Auntie is still using
social media for the elderly.

696
00:40:49,600 --> 00:40:50,640
Do you know about Reels?

697
00:40:50,760 --> 00:40:53,360
Don't lecture us if you don't, old hag.

698
00:40:53,560 --> 00:40:54,600
You won't understand now.

699
00:40:54,840 --> 00:40:57,160
In a few years, you'll know how
childish this is.

700
00:40:57,280 --> 00:40:59,240
Yes, that's why we want to have fun now.

701
00:40:59,400 --> 00:41:00,640
That's being young.

702
00:41:00,920 --> 00:41:02,520
Why don't you join us?

703
00:41:02,640 --> 00:41:04,480
Maybe you'll rejuvenate and can walk again.

704
00:41:04,600 --> 00:41:06,760
I'm not interested, I only want to know

705
00:41:06,920 --> 00:41:09,160
who told you to imitate Ngai Ka-yan
and make these videos.

706
00:41:10,160 --> 00:41:11,520
Why should I tell you?

707
00:41:13,080 --> 00:41:14,040
Police!

708
00:41:14,600 --> 00:41:16,840
Let's split...
Bye, bye, officers!

709
00:41:19,200 --> 00:41:22,920
Miss Lok, you're out on bail,
don't be reckless.

710
00:41:23,280 --> 00:41:26,080
You're here because you saw the new logo.

711
00:41:26,400 --> 00:41:30,360
I told you it's YIO and not IOY.

712
00:41:30,720 --> 00:41:32,280
Whoever orchestrated this

713
00:41:32,400 --> 00:41:34,320
is likely to be connected to
Ngai Ka-yan's death.

714
00:41:34,720 --> 00:41:35,720
Never mind that now.

715
00:41:35,920 --> 00:41:37,840
You know your mother is worried about you.

716
00:41:38,040 --> 00:41:39,120
Let's find the real killer together.

717
00:41:40,760 --> 00:41:43,040
In the past few months, I drilled my Mom

718
00:41:43,120 --> 00:41:44,360
about the details of the swap.

719
00:41:44,480 --> 00:41:45,800
She couldn't have done it.

720
00:41:45,840 --> 00:41:47,880
She didn't kill Ngai Ka-yan.

721
00:41:48,400 --> 00:41:50,000
Gogo Sir, I found something.

722
00:41:50,360 --> 00:41:52,120
I remember the trick these kids pulled.

723
00:41:52,200 --> 00:41:53,920
Ngai Ka-yan did it before.
It was a trending topic.

724
00:41:54,160 --> 00:41:56,600
I checked the three videos they posted.

725
00:41:56,680 --> 00:41:59,400
They were all trending videos
by Ngai Ka-yan.

726
00:42:00,160 --> 00:42:02,800
Neighbor Vs Stink Bomb, 385,000 views.

727
00:42:03,120 --> 00:42:05,840
Live from Sorry Sir, 420,000 views.

728
00:42:06,400 --> 00:42:10,120
Pigswill Life A or B, 455,000 views.

729
00:42:10,440 --> 00:42:13,960
Tangled Shoelaces, 480,000 views.

730
00:42:14,560 --> 00:42:16,520
That many?

731
00:42:16,840 --> 00:42:19,600
They put Ngai Ka-yan's videos
on a ranking list.

732
00:42:19,760 --> 00:42:23,280
That means, if we follow the
most popular video,

733
00:42:23,320 --> 00:42:24,560
we'll be able to find those kids.

734
00:42:25,720 --> 00:42:28,120
Yes, but the problem is,

735
00:42:28,520 --> 00:42:31,480
the video with the highest viewership
is the Static Apnea Challenge.

736
00:42:33,800 --> 00:42:36,400
They want to do another death on livestream?
